{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 9: a meteor apocalypse",
 "summary": "Three futuristic towers modelled from cubes (loop cuts, bevelled corners, a stepped top) with a voronoi window material and red rooftops, collected and instanced on the edges of a street grid (Mesh to Points on edges, Collection Info with Pick Instance, random Z rotation); Realize Instances and Split Edges so every face is loose, and Set Position pushing the faces out along their captured normals by a Geometry Proximity to the meteor through a Map Range: the buildings burst where the meteor is. The meteor in nodes: a subdivided, jittered cube with a noise-driven fire emission, its faces from index 92 extruded into a tail turned into billowing smoke (Mesh to Volume, Distribute Points in Volume, Points to Volume, Volume to Mesh, a Principled Volume). Beyond the tutorial: the meteor animated falling in at dusk, the city bursting as it lands.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "Metropolis",
   "description": "the city"
  },
  {
   "name": "Meteor",
   "description": "the meteor"
  }
 ],
 "expected_result": "A dusk city of blue glass towers on a street grid; a blazing meteor with a smoky tail plunges in and the towers around it burst apart.",
